WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:11.220
The history of gaming extends 5,000 years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.720
Ancient games foretold the futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.200
They were magic ceremonies that determined a person's fate.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.340
These ceremonies were known as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.990
In the present, a young boy solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.210
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.300
This boy possesses two hearts - one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.210
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.340
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.250
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.000
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.700
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.800
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.170
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:26.100
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.350
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:39.620
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:46.360
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.840
It's been a while, Yugi and Jonouchi.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.520
Dinosaur Ryuzaki?

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.500
You're Mai's servant?

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.530
That's pointless.  Finish him with Nightmare Shadow Sonic!

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.210
What?  He reflected back my Shadow Sonic?

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.720
My Lava Battleguard!

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.290
Honda's card saved me.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.170
Thank you, Honda.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:36.740
Black Flame!  Red-Eyes B. Dragon

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.740
I play this monster in defense position.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.010
Go, Lava Battleguard!

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.640
Good, Jonouchi.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.400
Since the two Battleguards are increasing each other's powers, now's your chance!

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.720
Go, Jonouchi!

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:11.050
Show that dino freak the power of our friendship!

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.470
The power of friendship?  Don't make me laugh!

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.130
My strongest card is still in my deck.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.720
My most powerful card has arrived!

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.350
Come out, Red-Eyes B. Dragon!

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:29.590
What?

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.370
Red-Eyes?

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.960
It's rare that anyone gets to see this card.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.250
You should feel proud to lose to this card.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:53.800
I've never seen Red-Eyes B. Dragon before.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.950
It's a legendary rare card that rivals Blue-Eyes.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:01.450
Who knew Ryuzaki had such a card?

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:06.600
It took all my savings to get this super rare card.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:12.200
I add the spell card Dragon Nails to power it up.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.210
Go, Red-Eyes!  Black Fireball!

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.970
Me and Honda's Battleguards were destroyed!

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:34.280
Your lame friendship didn't amount to much.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.890
Damn!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.880
My servant isn't so bad when he actually tries.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.570
Jonouchi, it's your turn.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.040
Is this the end?

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.770
Jonouchi!

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.880
Yugi, is there a way that Jonouchi can win?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.910
Or is he going to lose?

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.920
For Jonouchi to win in this situation...

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.980
There's only one possible way.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:09.320
But I promised I wouldn't give Jonouchi any advice.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:15.820
Jonouchi, it's impossible for an amateur like you to defeat me.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:20.080
I don't have any monsters that can defeat Ryuzaki's.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.200
Am I going to lose?

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.300
Don't give up, Jonouchi!

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.540
You're not the type who gives up!

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.560
That's right, Jonouchi.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.280
Hang in there!  There has to be a way to win!

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.170
Believe in yourself, Jonouchi!

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:46.010
Jonouchi, there's no way you can defeat me-

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.730
Actually, Jonouchi set his Time Wizard card.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:57.550
Time Wizard's Time Magic is a wild card because no one knows what it will cause.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:01.240
But I bet he doesn't even know that he can use it.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.880
Servant, finish him off!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:11.210
Wait.  This amateur used Time Wizard to beat Mai Kujaku.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:17.820
So if I acquire Time Wizard, there's no way I'll lose to Mai.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.520
Jonouchi!

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.960
How about the winner of this duel gets to take one rare card from the loser?

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:29.770
If I win, I get your Time Wizard.  Got it?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.940
Time Wizard?

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.670
Oh yeah.  I placed it on the field.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:40.170
In exchange, I'll give you my Red-Eyes if I lose.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.750
What?  You must be joking!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.250
Ryuzaki, I won't allow you to make up new rules!

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.800
Be quiet!

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.990
You're my servant, so you have to listen to my commands!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.480
I'm not your servant!

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.760
Don't act like you're better than me!

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.480
How dare you!

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:00.160
What's going on?  Red-Eyes is a super rare card.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.510
If he's willing to wager it...

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:06.510
Time Wizard must be even more valuable than that.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:13.630
I can't imagine what will happen if I use this card, but...

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:19.090
Fine, Ryuzaki.  If I lose this duel, I'll let you have my Time Wizard.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.750
All right!

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.970
Jonouchi?

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:24.360
It'll be mine.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:29.030
But before then, I'm using the card!

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.530
What?

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.240
He realized that it's his only chance!

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.490
That idiot!  He should've kept his mouth shut!

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.920
It's not over yet!

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:51.360
The odds of Time Magic activating is one in two.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.390
You're not good enough to master Time Wizard.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.890
Time Roulette!

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.200
The roulette has started to spin.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:05.920
Success means Time Magic.  Failure means self-destruction.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.530
C'mon, hit the mark!

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.780
The needle...

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.010
...is stopping.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.730
Success!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.760
Time Magic!

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.830
Time Magic!

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.730
What's going to happen?

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:06.930
Yugi, look.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.050
What's this?

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.290
What happened?

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:32.410
Millions of years have passed in an instant, so Red-Eyes has turned into a fossil.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.090
My Red-Eyes...

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.010
Ryuzaki!

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:44.690
As you promised, I'll take your Star Chips and Red-Eyes.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.730
All right! Jonouchi won!

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.640
Honda!

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:52.870
Jonouchi!

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.240
Honda!

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:55.920
Jonouchi!

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.280
Honda-

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:03.420
I feel much better now.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:07.750
You punk!  You came back here to punch me?

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.950
That's what you get for making me worry.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:14.600
I'm not in such bad shape that I need someone like you to worry about me!

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:15.640
What did you say?

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:16.630
You wanna fight?

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:19.320
Knock it off, Jonouchi and Honda.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.360
Leave them be, Yugi.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.080
That's how they communicate.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:26.010
Really?

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:30.970
But they really are Lava and Swamp Dummies.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.880
It's gotten dark.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:38.120
I don't see any other duelists around.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:41.440
No one's going to duel at night.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.760
What should we do?

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:44.920
Let's find a place to sleep outdoors.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:49.130
We have to do that?  Not cool.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.850
I'm starving!

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:18.360
I can't believe they invited us to a tournament and didn't provide any food.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:21.810
Well, Yugi was the only one who was invited.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:26.020
Right now, I want potato chips instead of Star Chips!

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:28.400
I want to take a relaxing bath.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:30.880
I found a mushroom!

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.680
Time to eat!

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:34.420
No!  It's definitely poisonous!

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.700
You'll get sick, Jonouchi.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:40.780
Oh my, you look like you're starving.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:43.490
You again?

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:51.390
You came here to show off your food?

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:56.330
Jonouchi, want to trade your Star Chips for this chocolate?

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:02.520
You must be joking!  These Star Chips are my life!

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:04.500
I was only kidding.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:08.840
I never thought you'd fall that far as a duelist.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:12.660
If personality were looks, you'd be one ugly girl.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:16.120
Let's not fight for one night.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.410
We both need our rest.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:22.480
You're right.  We're pretty tired from dueling all day.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.600
I don't trust her.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.170
Are you up to something?

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:30.330
So you don't need any dinner?

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.520
Wow!

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.040
Food, tent and a lantern?  She has everything!

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:39.270
You brought this all by yourself?

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.800
A duelist doesn't rely on others.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.160
That's why I'm prepared.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:46.240
You do the cooking.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.350
Sure.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:49.720
You two fetch water.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:50.640
Okay.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:53.480
It's super annoying that she's ordering me around.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:56.880
We're getting food out of this, idiot.  Deal with it.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:58.880
I'll get firewood.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:12:59.790
Okay.

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:02.650
You're Anzu, right?

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:07.600
There's a shower over there, so you can use it when they return with the water.

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:08.800
Really?

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.840
There are necessities that only women can understand.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.840
I'm starving.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:16.850
Is it ready yet?

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:23.920
I thought Mai Kujaku was annoying, but she does have some good points.

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:27.240
You guys, no peeking!

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.000
Keep cooking.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.440
Anzu, I'll stand guard outside, so don't worry.

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:33.800
Thank you.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:36.330
You don't need to thank me.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:44.860
Mai, why did you come to this island?

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:47.050
Is it for the prize money?

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:54.570
I traveled around the world as a casino dealer on a cruise ship.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.490
Day after day, I played cards with the wealthy.

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:03.610
They all used their money and power to show off.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:09.410
Gradually, I became sick of people.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.370
Hey.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:14.670
Why are you all here together?

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:17.480
Why?  Because we're friends.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:23.580
It's funny.  When I look at you guys, I feel like I'll remember something that I lost.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.080
Mai...

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.580
What is it?

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:30.050
I heard something behind the curtain.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.120
There's no one here.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.490
What's wrong?

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.640
Did something happen?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.570
Can I come in?

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.260
Of course not!

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:47.070
Looks delicious!

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.690
Thanks for the meal!

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:50.920
Hot!

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:52.440
Delicious!

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.440
Yeah, it's delicious.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:55.970
Yeah.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.880
Mai, you already have eight Star Chips?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.360
You might be the first one into the castle tomorrow.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.240
Yeah.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:10.410
But I want to battle you someday, Yugi.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:14.640
Let's forget about dueling for now.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.570
Yeah.  That kind of talk will spoil our dinner.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:21.920
We're sitting together for now, but you're my enemies tomorrow.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.090
That's what dueling is all about.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.280
I finished eating.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.450
I'm going to get some fresh air.

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:36.890
There's nothing charming about her.

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:55.940
It's not like me to reminisce about the past.

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:10.040
We should sleep.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:11.760
Where did Mai go?

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:12.840
Yeah.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.840
She does whatever she pleases.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.120
Leave her be.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.490
But...

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:19.880
Anzu?

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.040
Who's there?  Come on out!

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.130
If you won't, we're going in!

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:29.940
Bakura.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:34.270
That means I wasn't hallucinating.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.360
You secretly boarded the ship too?

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:39.760
Yes.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:42.080
We must've kept missing each other.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:47.370
I see.  Well, it's great that we have more support.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:53.430
What?  Everyone brought their cards?

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:55.030
What do you expect?

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:58.320
This is a kingdom for duelists, after all.

00:16:58.320 --> 00:16:59.270
Yeah.

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:03.270
Everyone on this island is putting their hearts into their cards.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:05.080
That was corny!

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:08.370
What's your favorite card, Jonouchi?

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:10.920
This one, of course.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:14.680
Call me Flame Swordsman from now on!

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:17.880
My favorite is Cyber Commander!

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:20.240
You guys act like little kids.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.000
But Jonouchi's right.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.660
Anzu, you must have a favorite card.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:26.630
Well...

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:28.630
This is my favorite card.

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:31.000
What?  Magician of Faith?

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.440
She looks suspicious.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:34.650
You idiot!

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:38.240
What's your favorite card, Yugi?

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.740
Dark Magician, of course.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:47.880
I'm starting to understand how it feels to believe in your favorite cards and duel.

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:51.410
Grandpa always talked about the heart of the cards.

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:56.290
You can't truly duel until you play with cards that have your heart.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.360
What's your favorite card, Bakura?

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.610
This one.

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.830
Change of Heart?

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.770
That's a weird card to like.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.680
Yugi, will you duel me?

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:15.440
But not for Star Chips, of course.

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:17.880
That sounds fun, Yugi.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:21.840
Since coming to the island, it's been one serious battle after another.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:22.960
You're right.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:25.550
It would be nice to take a break and have a casual duel.

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:31.060
What if you put your favorite cards into Yugi's deck?

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:32.560
That's a great idea.

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.060
Yeah.

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:38.330
All right.  Let's put in all your cards and make an original deck.

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:48.360
Okay, we're ready.

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:50.590
Good luck, you two.

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:54.080
I don't think you can beat Yugi, but do your best, Bakura.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.130
Yeah.

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:05.560
What?

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.970
What's that sound?

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:14.050
That's...

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.810
What's going on?

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:23.290
This is a Shadow Game!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:47.130
This was too easy.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:55.290
The Millennium Puzzle is mine.

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.210
What?

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:10.930
I'll face you in this Shadow Game.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:14.630
The other Yugi has shown up.

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:17.250
I've been waiting for you.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:37.220
Why is everyone cosplaying as Duel Monsters?

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:39.190
I'm cosplaying too?

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:43.200
Bakura's power trapped us into a game.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:46.520
We can't return to normal unless we win the game.

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:48.260
This must be a dream.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:49.960
Everyone, let's go!

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:54.360
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Morphing Jar's Trap!
Flame Swordsman in Danger

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:56.210
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:09.720
The flask glistens

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:17.570
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:26.550
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:34.320
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:40.140
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:44.270
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:52.540
I will support your lonely back

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:56.780
Shower of happiness

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:00.900
You are not alone

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:07.620
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
